 61MN    COULOMB EXCITATION:XUNDL-3    2009VA16                           200906
 61MN c  Beam={+61}Mn, target={+109}Ag                                          
 61MN c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2009Va16:                          
 61MN c  Eur Phys J A (in press 2009; available online June 9, 2009;            
 61MN2c  Van de Walle et al.)                                                   
 61MN c  Compiled by B. Karamy and B. Singh (McMaster), June 24, 2009           
 61MN c  2.87 MeV/nucleon beam of {+61}Mn was produced in fission of            
 61MN2c  uranium (UC{-x} target) induced by 1.4 GeV protons from PS Booster     
 61MN3c  at CERN. The laser ionized (RILIS facility at ISOLDE-CERN) Mn isotopes 
 61MN4c  were extracted from the ion source and mass separated. The 30-keV      
 61MN5c  isobaric beam was bunched in a Penning trap (REXTRAP) and injected     
 61MN6c  in the electron beam ion source (EBIS). The {+61}Mn beam was           
 61MN7c  accelerated to 2.87 MeV/nucleon and impinged on a {+109}Ag target.     
 61MN c  Measured E|g, I|g,|g(|q) using MINIBALL Ge detector array. Deduced     
 61MN2c  B(E2) value using GOSIA analysis. Comparison with shell-model          
 61MN3c  calculations. The data were normalized to excitations in the target    
 61MN4c  nucleus {+109}Ag                                                       
 61MN cG E$ From 2008Va08                                                       
 61MN cL E,J$ From 2008Va08                                                     
